*About Finova Motors*

Finova Motors is an emerging SpaceTech and DeepTech company developing advanced motor technologies and satellite subsystems, including Reaction Wheels and Control Moment Gyroscopes (CMGs), which are critical components of satellite Attitude Determination and Control Systems (ADCS).

We are focused on building indigenous technologies with applications across the space, aerospace, defence, EV and robotics sectors.

*About the Role*

We are looking for proactive, organised and enthusiastic individuals to join our Founder's Office.

The role primarily involves providing administrative, documentation and coordination support to the founding team and assisting with the day-to-day requirements of a growing startup.

Working in a startup environment will also provide an opportunity to observe how different business functions operate and gain a basic understanding of entrepreneurship, business management and organisational processes.

*Key Responsibilities*

- Assisting with day-to-day administrative and clerical activities.
- Organising documents, maintaining records and managing data.
- Coordinating meetings, appointments and follow-ups.
- Preparing basic reports, presentations and documentation.
- Assisting with emails, communication and correspondence.
- Supporting information collection, online research and data compilation.
- Maintaining trackers, databases and internal records.
- Providing coordination support for events, meetings and other organisational activities.
- Assisting the founders with routine operational and administrative requirements.

*Who Should Apply?*

- Students or recent graduates from any academic background.
- Individuals interested in entrepreneurship, startups and business management.
- Good communication and basic computer skills.
- Organised, responsible and attentive to detail.
- Willingness to learn, take initiative and adapt to a dynamic work environment.
- Ability to manage multiple tasks and follow through on responsibilities.

*No prior work experience is required. We value curiosity, sincerity and a willingness to learn.*

*What You Will Gain*

- An opportunity to work in a growing SpaceTech startup.
- Familiarity with startup administration and organisational processes.
- Exposure to different business functions and workplace practices.
- An opportunity to interact with the founding team and understand the startup ecosystem.
- Practical experience in communication, documentation, coordination and professional work practices.
- A chance to develop organisational skills, professional confidence and workplace discipline.

*A stipend will be provided during the internship.*

If you are looking to gain your first professional experience in a dynamic startup environment and are eager to learn, we would love to hear from you!


